From d1ed232aa04d4097103fee52be0e3a9c070f2503 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:58:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v3.0.9: low-hanging fruit - six backlog items that needed no
 field data

- Wireless Quality (Reaper_Wireless.asp): Lock/Unlock restart the radio the
  admin is usually on, and the single 18 s fetch landed mid-outage, so a lock
  that worked looked like it did nothing. refreshWhenBack() polls
  /httpd_check.xml with backoff (12 s, x1.5, 15 s cap, 20 tries) and repaints
  twice; RWIF_94 says so if the router never answers (x25 dicts).
- Gatekeeper (web.c do_reaper_gk_cgi status): seen.tsv is gkd's first-sight
  snapshot and could say Wired for a wireless client. Load the live cfg_mnt
  client lists once per request and let a wireless hit that is not listed
  wired override band/wired - on a copy, the static record stays gkd's.
  Display only; enforcement is by MAC.
- rwatch check 3c: a MISSING Warden chain while Warden is enabled is
  re-applied under the firewall lock, once per 10 min, logged, with the
  warden-chain-missing token - the end state of the stuck-nvram path behind
  the BE92U addon-box report (the defensive half; root cause still owes
  the tester's syslog).
- Dashboard: the per-band device list caps at four rows and scrolls
  (max-height 254px); five orphaned style blocks removed after a cross-page
  usage check (arrow, railsearch, rc-sec, spark, speeds).
- rexport: MAC masking applies one sed script instead of one rewrite per MAC.
- amaspark: four radio slots, so the GT-BE98 family's fourth carrier is part
  of the MLO link-set handling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
